hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1078","Chapter on what is owed of obedience to commanders and of refusing them when they command disobedience, 1116 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ya'la ibn Muslim informed me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that he said: O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you - it was revealed concerning Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah ibn Qays ibn Adi al-Sahmi, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him out with an expedition."
"1079","1117 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hearing and obeying are binding upon the Muslim man unless he is commanded to disobey Allah. When he is commanded to disobey, there is neither hearing nor obeying."
